# Normalize line endings to LF.
#
# Upstream and CI always check out LF, but a Windows contributor with the default
# core.autocrlf=true gets CRLF in the working tree. That makes local Biome/lint
# results disagree with CI, and shell scripts fail in WSL/Git Bash with $'\r'.
# The eol attribute takes precedence over core.autocrlf, so this keeps every
# working copy on LF. The index already stores LF, so this adds no content diff.
* text=auto eol=lf
